w: 1.~When Is- r'el out of E- gypt went, and did his dwell- ing change, When Ja- cob's house went out from those that _ were of lang- uage strange,
w: 2.~He Ju- dah did his sanc- tua- ry, his king- dom Is- r'el make: The sea it saw, and quick- ly fled, Jor- _ dan was dri- ven back.
w: 3.~Like rams the moun- tains, and like lambs the hills skipped to and fro. O sea, why fledd'st thou? Jor- dan, back why _ wast thou dri- ven so?
w: 4.~Ye moun- tains great, where- fore was it that ye did skip like rams? And where- fore was it, lit- tle hills, that _ ye did leap like lambs?
w: 5.~O at the pre- sence of the Lord, earth, trem- ble thou for fear, While as the pre- sence of the God of _ Ja- cob doth ap- pear:
w: 6.~Who from the hard and sto- ny rock did stand- ing wa- ter bring; And by his pow'r did turn the flint in- _ to a wa- ter\-- spring.
